    "faq": {
      "title": "Frequently asked questions",
      "items": [
        {
          "question": "How are plans priced?",
          "answer": "Every plan is billed per user, per workspace. Starter is ₹500 monthly, or ₹425/user/month on yearly (15% off). Premium is ₹1,000 monthly, or ₹850/user/month on yearly (15% off). Enterprise starts from ₹12L per year."
        },
        {
          "question": "Which plans include billing?",
          "answer": "All of them. Starter, Premium, and Enterprise are billed per user, per workspace — not one bill for the whole team."
        },
        {
          "question": "How many people and booking pages do I get?",
          "answer": "Starter is 1–5 people and 1 booking page with an Indlio watermark. Premium is 2–50 people and unlimited booking pages, with no watermark. Enterprise is 50+ people and unlimited booking pages, with no watermark."
        },
        {
          "question": "What's on Premium that Starter does not have?",
          "answer": "Multi-currency, multi-timezone, custom forms, the customer portal, unlimited integrations, and standard reports start on Premium. Starter includes 10 integrations, basic reports, and an Indlio watermark on the booking page. Every plan is billed per user, per workspace."
        },
        {
          "question": "What's the difference between Premium and Enterprise?",
          "answer": "Premium is for one studio that shares a calendar, up to 50 people, unlimited booking pages, and the standard reports. Enterprise adds custom reports, workflows, and multi-location access, plus SSO and SAML, Salesforce and Dynamics, domain control, audit logs, a data deletion API, onboarding and implementation, and dedicated account support."
        },
        {
          "question": "Do I need a credit card to join?",
          "answer": "No. The waitlist is an email. We'll contact you when Indlio Bookings is ready for the first SMEs."
        },
        {
          "question": "Can I switch plans later?",
          "answer": "Yes. Start on Starter and move to Premium or Enterprise when the workspace grows."
        }
      ]
